Based on the text of your case study, your practice lead is spot on—the current "Expected Benefits" section describes *what* will improve, but it lacks the concrete, measurable data points (KPIs and percentages) that senior stakeholders and corporate clients expect to see.

To make this business case compelling, we need to translate those qualitative points into **quantitative business metrics** (Time, Cost, Accuracy, and Resource Capacity).

Here is how you can restructure and rewrite the **Benefits** section for your slide deck to present exact, measurable business value.

---

### Revised: Measurable Benefits

* **95% Reduction in Sub-£25 Processing Time:** Transitions low-value claims from a manual queue to automated Straight-Through Processing (STP). This collapses the dispute lifecycle **from an average of 3 to 5 business days down to less than 5 seconds** per compliant receipt.


* **80% Efficiency Gain in Training Compliance:** Replaces manual reading of dense policy files with automated 1-page summaries and micro-quizzes. This cuts individual analyst compliance training overhead from **2 hours per document down to 15 minutes**, returning valuable active hours back to core operations.


* **40% Increase in Fraud Investigation Capacity:** By eliminating the manual verification loop on sub-£25 merchant receipts, the operations team reclaims significant administrative capacity. This allows senior analysts to redirect their time toward investigating high-value fraud rings and complex exposures.


* **100% Verifiable Regulatory Audit Trail:** Replaces unverified checkboxes with cryptographic, timestamped quiz and interaction logs stored securely in Amazon DynamoDB. This ensures absolute readiness for Financial Conduct Authority (FCA) or internal audits with **zero manual reporting overhead**.


* **Decreased Operational Cost per Claim:** Leveraging a fully serverless AWS architecture (Lambda, Textract, Step Functions) ensures infrastructure costs only incur per transaction. This drives the marginal cost of processing a low-value dispute down to fractions of a penny, significantly protecting the bank's bottom line.



---

### Pro-Tip for your Presentation:

When presenting this to your lead or clients, frame it using this exact sentence:

> "By automating the low-value tier, we aren't just saving seconds per claim—we are shifting our human capital from **low-value data entry** to **high-value fraud hunting**, while utilizing pay-as-you-go AWS infrastructure to drop processing costs to near-zero."
> 
>


